            "Description": "A parent compound is conceptually the \"important\" part of the molecule when the molecule has more than one covalent component. Specifically, a parent component must have at least one carbon and contain at least 70% of the heavy (non-hydrogen) atoms of all the unique covalent units (ignoring stoichiometry). Note that this is a very empirical definition and is subject to change.",
