                "TOCHeading": "FIFRA Requirements",
                "Description": "The Federal Insecticide, Fungicide, and Rodenticide Act (FIFRA) is the Federal statute that governs the registration, distribution, sale, and use of pesticides in the United States.",
                "URL": "https://www.epa.gov/enforcement/federal-insecticide-fungicide-and-rodenticide-act-fifra-and-federal-facilities",
                "Information": [
                  {
                    "ReferenceNumber": 24,
                    "Description": "PEER REVIEWED",
                    "Reference": [
                      "40 CFR 180.3(e) (USEPA); U.S. National Archives and Records Administration's Electronic Code of Federal Regulations. Available from, as of March 2, 2010: https://www.ecfr.gov"
                    ],
                    "ExtendedReference": [
                      {
                        "Citation": "40 CFR 180.3(e) (USEPA); U.S. National Archives and Records Administration's Electronic Code of Federal Regulations. Available from, as of March 2, 2010: https://www.ecfr.gov",
