                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "TERRESTRIAL FATE: Based on a classification scheme(1), Koc values of 308-1158(2) indicate that zineb is expected to have low to moderate mobility in soil(SRC). Volatilization of zineb from moist soil surfaces is not expected to be an important fate process since zineb is a zinc salt(SRC). Zineb is not expected to volatilize from dry soil surfaces(SRC) based upon a vapor pressure of <7.5X10-8 mm Hg(3). Zineb field half-lives range from 23-43 days(4). Dithiocarbamate fungicides undergo rapid decomposition in the presence of moisture(5-6); therefore, zineb decomposition in and on wet soil may be an important fate process(SRC).",
                          "Markup": [
                            {
                              "Start": 95,
                              "Length": 5,
                              "URL": "https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/zineb",
