                      },
                      {
                        "Citation": "(2) Vanhemmen JJ et al; Meded Fac Landbouwwet, Univ Gent 57(3B): 1269-83 (1992)"
                      }
                    ],
                    "Value": {
                      "StringWithMarkup": [
                        {
                          "String": "Concentrations of dithiocarbamate fungicides in the workroom air of a pesticide residue laboratory were below the provisional threshold level value of 5 mg/cu m(1). This provisional threshold level value of 5 mg/cu m in the workroom air was based on the TLV officially stated for thiram. It has been adopted for all dithiocarbamate fungicides by the company in this study (name of company not disclosed)(1). The levels of dermal exposure of greenhouse workers handling carnations was studied in the Netherlands(2). Average dermal exposure to zineb was 48 mg/task while cutting and 8 mg/task  while sorting/bundling(2). Inhalation exposure to zineb was 0.6 mg/task while cutting while no exposure was calculated during sorting/bundling(2).",
                          "Markup": [
